This is crazy. ml-intern just passed the @huggingface internship test in 15 minutes. The task was to replicate a research baseline from a DeepMind paper on test-time compute scaling. The agent read the DeepMind paper, focused on Appendix E, selected the right scoring strategy, ran 16 solutions per problem through a reward model, grouped by final answer, summed scores, and picked the winner, achieving a 20 percentage point increase in accuracy from 45% to 65%.

It generated four plots, pushed a full results dataset to the Hub, and deployed a Docker Space on a T4 GPU. The funniest part is that it cited @lewtun's code snippet as a reference, and it also wrote the README, documented every design decision with paper citations, and added a co-authorship note explaining its contributions.

