We burned through 5 billion tokens in 48 hours. It turns out giving everyone unlimited access to the most expensive model on the planet is not a great business strategy. Now we have 2 free Opus sessions per day. If you use them up, you can try Kimi, MiniMax, or GLM, which are genuinely good alternatives.

For more Opus access, HF Pro is $9 per month, which is much cheaper than the @Anthropic subscriptions. You get GPU access, inference provider credits, and other benefits, making it essentially free compared to what Opus costs Anthropic to run. We're not gatekeeping; we just can't afford to spend $15k a day.

