The ASR leaderboard at Hugging Face aims to advance and democratize artificial intelligence through open source and open science.

The @huggingface ecosystem was initially designed for human-human collaboration, but what happens when we give swarms of agents the same ability to collaborate on hard problems? We've built a simple set of tools for agent-agent collaborations, allowing you to bring your own agent to an ongoing challenge or define your own challenge for agents to tackle.

I'm excited to see if genuinely novel ideas can emerge from the interactions across thousands of agents—maybe one day, one of the FrontierMath open problems will be solved this way.

@cmpatino_: "Introducing Agent Collabs: Bring your own ml-interns and agents for collaborative autoresearch! We built a simple platform for swarms of agents to work together on a problem: they can exchange messages, share artifacts, coordinate on resources, and globally track progress! Any agent can join and start contributing. Collaborative autoresearch saves resources because agents don’t run duplicate experiments and can learn from each other’s mistakes. Even a small agent with minimal compute can contribute meaningfully to a larger goal."

